description:
GOAL
Build the shared E2E execution/logging substrate used by every capability bead: scripts/e2e/lib.sh, scripts/e2e/run_all.sh, schema validation, failure preservation, and self-tests. It supplies mechanics only; it cannot make dormant full/release lanes green or substitute for real subsystem tests.

DELIVERABLES
- lib.sh APIs for step execution, assertions, digest/resource/obligation capture, deterministic seed/replay, secret-safe command display, cleanup and failure-state preservation;
- every script runs in strict shell mode and emits each setup/action/assertion/failpoint/cleanup step to stderr and an artifact as valid NDJSON;
- base required fields: schema version, timestamp/logical sequence, revision/toolchain/target/features/profile, script and stable acceptance ID, step, seed/schedule/failpoint, secret-safe command digest, exit/duration, expected/actual typed result, authority/generation/policy position where applicable, resource/obligation deltas, artifact/log digests, and replay command. Domain beads add their own typed fields;
- terminal record carries discovered assertions, passed/failed/skipped/unsupported counts and exact IDs, first-attempt outcome, cleanup/containment state, wall time and artifact directory;
- run_all.sh executes selected scripts without hiding stderr, validates every record and terminal row, preserves first attempts, aggregates exact sets and artifacts, and returns nonzero on any failure, malformed/truncated/missing terminal log, timeout, orphan/containment failure, zero assertion, or required unsupported/skipped result;
- harness self-tests cover every library function and plant command failure, assertion mismatch, malformed NDJSON, truncated stream, missing terminal row, zero assertions, duplicate ID, timeout, and cleanup failure;
- comment header in lib.sh is the canonical usage reference; no separate process document.

ACCEPTANCE
Harness self-tests exercise both positive and planted-negative paths. The harness can prove its own mechanics only; running one self-test or any minimum script count is never release coverage. FG-091 independently owns the exact expected-suite manifest and full/release activation, including required-set equality. Until real suites and FG-091 land, full/release retain typed dormant exit 3.

UNIT/PORTABILITY TESTS
bash syntax and declared shell/static checks; paths with spaces/Unicode; concurrent log writers; interrupted/partial files; deterministic seed; secret redaction; signal handling; artifact collisions; platform timestamp/tool differences; aggregation ordering; no Python or other tool is assumed unless registry-approved and checked by the constitution lane.

NON-CLAIMS
This bead contains no subsystem fixture presented as product proof, no CI correctness logic, and no auto-generated allowlist derived from discovered scripts.

GOAL
Make the final-abstraction, first-party-safe-only, and transitive trust-surface rules mechanically enforceable before the workspace expands.

DELIVERABLES
- conservative empty/placeholder crate detector: refuse crate roots containing only attributes/comments/TODO/unimplemented stubs or marker scaffolds with no real slice/tests, without pretending the heuristic proves architectural quality;
- crate/layer inventory and workspace-root coverage so every first-party target declares #![forbid(unsafe_code)] and no nested lockfile escapes inspection;
- unsafe_ledger registry schema and generated report for every enabled external/transitive unsafe block, generated expansion where practicable, soundness/advisory evidence, exact feature reachability, owner, containment, and removal/update path;
- build-script and proc-macro inventory with checked source/output fingerprints and authority-sensitive expansion goldens;
- WASM rule: there is no first-party exception. wasm-bindgen/framework-generated unsafe is transitive/generated dependency surface; a first-party lint relaxation, unsafe shim, or unreviewed expansion fails.

ACCEPTANCE
- planted empty, TODO-only, unsafe, lint-relaxation, extern-C, inline-assembly, nested-lockfile, build-script, proc-macro, and generated-WASM drift fixtures fail for stable typed reasons;
- a real minimal vertical slice passes;
- every enabled allow_fundamental/allow_by_audit/FrankenSuite dependency has matching unsafe/build/macro evidence, including target-specific feature closures;
- generated report distinguishes first-party source, proc-macro output, dependency source, and unreachable code; absence of a credited scan is not a pass;
- unit tests cover parser/graph edge cases; scripts/e2e/crate_graph_constitution.sh exercises planted negatives with detailed NDJSON and joins the exact release-suite manifest.

E2E LOGGING
Use scripts/e2e/lib.sh and set -euo pipefail. Log source/toolchain/target/feature/lock digests, fixture, command, exit, duration, expected/actual diagnostic, scanned targets/files, and final totals to stderr and an artifact. Preserve replay commands and checker output on failure.

CONSTITUTIONAL CONSTRAINTS
Pure Rust, dated nightly, no first-party unsafe or local exceptions, no C/C++ FFI, foreign Git production path, alternate runtime, network build, or unpublished path dependency. This checker is a tripwire; human final-abstraction review remains required.

GOAL
The smallest complete semantic oracle for the entire canonical protocol: seals, intents, statement outcomes, net effects, decisions, refs, forge aggregates, outcome index, retention roots, and authority heads — as a pure, deterministic, no-I/O safe-Rust state machine (crate fgit-reference).

WHY / BACKGROUND
Every optimized implementation (per-core lanes, combiners, storage formats, indexes) must be trace-refinable to ONE reference semantics (plan §40.1/§40.5). Without an executable oracle, "correct" degrades into "what the implementation happens to do." The model is deliberately slow and simple; its only jobs are to be OBVIOUSLY right, replayable, and diffable. It is also the object FG-041's mechanized proofs will target, so keep its transition functions small and total.

MODEL SURFACE (from plan §10, §15, normative contract)
- TransactionSeal put-if-absent with byte-identical-retry / IdempotencyKeyReuse outcomes;
- ordered statements -> typed intents -> read-your-own-writes evaluation -> target-disjoint net-effect normal form (delegating detailed folding semantics to FG-008's component, which this crate hosts the interface for);
- DecisionSequence (every terminal admitted decision incl. refusals) vs RepositorySequence (committed transitions only) as distinct monotone sequences;
- RepositoryDecisionBatch/RepositoryCommitRecord/RepositoryAuthorityHead transitions with exact predecessor binding;
- CAS win/loss/ambiguity; cancellation semantics (no canonical Cancelled terminal; pre-seal vanish vs post-seal retryable);
- refusal taxonomy as typed values.

STRUCTURE: closes when subtasks (core model; golden traces + replay; exhaustive small-state campaign) close.

ACCEPTANCE (epic)
- no I/O, ambient time, randomized hash order, or runtime dependency (std only);
- operations consume an explicit snapshot and produce typed intents/effects/refusals;
- replay from genesis or any head yields byte-stable roots;
- model state serializes into golden traces via fg002 codec;
- a documented API by which implementation crates differential-test against this oracle.

FUTURE-SELF NOTES
Resist adding performance anything here — the model's slowness is a feature. When FG-041 mechanization arrives, any cleverness in these transition functions becomes proof debt.

CONSTITUTIONAL CONSTRAINTS (AGENTS.md; non-negotiable)
- Pure Rust, edition 2024, dated-nightly pin from rust-toolchain.toml; every first-party crate carries #![forbid(unsafe_code)]; no C/C++ FFI, no C Git/libgit2/JGit/Dulwich/gix, no hidden subprocess fallback. Upstream Git binaries are pinned, sandboxed differential ORACLES only (never production).
- Asupersync is the sole async runtime (no Tokio/async-std/smol). Long-lived work owns children via regions; cancellation is request -> drain -> finalize; effects use typed obligations (Reserved -> Committed -> Acknowledged, or Reserved -> Aborted).
- Closed dependency universe: every crate (incl. transitive, enforced via Cargo.lock scan) must match an active allow row in registries/dependency_policy.tsv. No build scripts/proc macros without a constitutional exception. No network during builds.
- Final-abstraction slices only: no empty crates, no HashMap-pretending-to-be-storage, no fixture-only parser wired as production API. A subset is fine when its unsupported surface is a typed refusal.
- Claim lattice (invariant > proof > bounded model > statistical > SLO > benchmark): never describe this work as stronger than its evidence. Record disproven hypotheses in docs/NEGATIVE_EVIDENCE_LEDGER.md + registries/negative_evidence.tsv.
- Run ./scripts/verify.sh fast before and after; stage only intended files; keep generated artifacts out of source.

---
## EMBEDDED NORMATIVE CONTENT (verbatim from the design docs; self-contained — do not consult the source markdown)

### The 28 minimum release-blocking invariants (NORMATIVE_PROTOCOL_CONTRACTS §32) — the reference model is the executable oracle for all of them

The mutation/storage core cannot be called complete until executable evidence covers at least:

1. one canonical `TxId` derivation and key-reuse mismatch rejection;
2. at most one terminal decision per sealed `TxId`;
3. lost response/cancellation cannot create two outcomes;
4. head generation/predecessor and decision/RCR sequence continuity;
5. one head CAS publishes ref and forge effects atomically;
6. CAS losers preserve the same sealed request;
7. expected-old/force/atomic semantics under races;
8. one pinned policy/configuration snapshot per attempt;
9. witness refinement only removes false conflicts;
10. no staged/quarantined object becomes a retention root before commit;
11. committed closure is protected before acknowledgement according to profile;
12. SHA-1 and SHA-256 cannot collide at the type boundary;
13. production cannot invoke/link an external Git engine;
14. every first-party crate forbids unsafe;
15. replica conflict lattices do not hide contradictory terminals;
16. generation activation is exact-predecessor and anti-rollback;
17. carried-forward checkpoint cannot masquerade as current forge position;
18. repaired bytes require original commitments and current-authority publication;
19. projection/search/graph lag cannot authorize mutation or deletion;
20. no mixed-generation Context Packet without explicit joined receipt;
21. GC cannot sweep authenticated, held, active, or grace roots;
22. outbox retry cannot duplicate canonical events;
23. all effect obligations settle at region close;
24. Git receive-pack conformance does not rely on fictional protocol-v2 push;
25. verifier independence class is enforced, not self-declared;
26. release manifest cannot publish a partial target matrix;
27. every commit/refusal is explainable from immutable evidence roots;
28. crash/replay at every staged/visible/durable boundary converges or fails closed.

### Two distinct monotone sequences (NORMATIVE §3 / plan §10.2)

- `DecisionSequence` orders every terminal admitted decision, INCLUDING refusals.
- `RepositorySequence` orders only committed repository-state transitions.
A refusal is canonical audit state consuming DecisionSequence but does NOT advance refs/forge/retention/RepositorySequence.

### Terminal outcome enum (NORMATIVE §5.3)

```rust
enum DecisionOutcome {
    Committed { repository_commit_id: RepositoryCommitId },
    Refused { code: RefusalCode, refusal_record_id: RefusalRecordId },
}
```

There is NO canonical `Cancelled` terminal outcome. Infrastructure interruption before publication leaves the sealed transaction undecided and retryable. Client cancellation cannot erase or redefine a decision. Pre-seal rejection (authentication failure, malformed framing, unsupported capability, resource violation, tenant suspension, coarse throttling) MAY reject before a seal exists, but such a response MUST NOT claim `Committed`/`Refused` or non-commit after an ambiguous attempt.

---
## PLAN-SPACE REVIEW REVISIONS (added during the pre-implementation polish pass)

- Scope-honesty note (claim lattice): the small-state campaign (fg003c) exercises 5 core properties at G0; witness-refinement (invariant 9) and mixed-generation (invariant 20) are exercised at their owning beads (fg025, fg064) not in the G0 model. The epic's "oracle for all 28 invariants" means the model DEFINES the semantics they are checked against, not that G0 alone tests all 28 — do not over-state.

comments.text:
PUBLISHED SURFACE (FG-004a vocabulary, frozen for wave 1) at commit b1803d7, crate fgit-authority.

OPS (crate::vocabulary::AuthorityOp, re-exported at crate root):
  PutIfAbsent { key: ImmutableKey, body: Vec<u8> }
  ReadImmutable { key: ImmutableKey }
  InitializeHead { key: HeadKey, generation: HeadGeneration, body: Vec<u8> }
  ReadHead { key: HeadKey }
  CompareExchangeHead { key: HeadKey, expected: AuthorityVersionToken, new_generation: HeadGeneration, new_body: Vec<u8> }
  AuthenticateHeadReceipt { receipt: HeadReadReceipt }
plus AuthorityOp::kind() -> AuthorityOpKind and AuthorityOp::is_mutating().

RESPONSES (AuthorityResponse): PutIfAbsent(PutOutcome) | ReadImmutable(ImmutableRead) | InitializeHead(HeadInit) | ReadHead(HeadRead) | CompareExchangeHead(CasOutcome) | AuthenticateHeadReceipt(AuthenticatedHead) | Refused(AuthorityRefusal) | Ambiguous(AmbiguityReason).
  PutOutcome = Created | IdenticalRetry | Conflict
  CasOutcome = Committed(HeadReadReceipt) | PredecessorMismatch
  HeadRead = Present(HeadReadReceipt) | Absent ; ImmutableRead = Present(Vec<u8>) | Absent
  HeadInit = Created(r) | IdenticalRetry(r) | Conflict

TOKENS: AuthorityVersionToken is opaque, Copy, 16 transport bytes, minted fresh per write, never content-derived, never reused. HeadGeneration strictly increases. StoreInstanceId separates endpoints; a token from one instance is UnknownVersionToken at another.

AMBIGUITY: AuthorityResponse::Ambiguous carries no outcome; response.proves_no_effect() is false for it by construction. Ground truth lives only in FaultLog (out of band). Resolution: resolve_ambiguous_cas / resolve_ambiguous_put.

For FG-004b (OliveFortress): AuthorityOp and AuthorityResponse are Clone+Debug+Eq, so History<AuthorityOp, AuthorityResponse> works unchanged. The invoke/return hook is trait AuthorityObserver { on_invoke(ClientId, step, &AuthorityOp); on_return(ClientId, step, &AuthorityResponse) } driven by drive(). src/history.rs and src/lincheck.rs mod lines are not yet wired into lib.rs — say the word and I add them.

description:
GOAL
Implement the embedded single-node AuthorityStore over the adopted FrankenSQLite engine while preserving exactly the same immutable-body and exact-predecessor head-CAS semantics as every other backend.

BOUNDARY
FrankenSQLite is permitted as (1) the embedded implementation of the one AuthorityStore and (2) disposable local projections. It is never a co-authoritative metadata database. SQL commit is canonical publication only inside the exact AuthorityStore operation; projection rows cannot authorize, retain, delete, or infer commit.

STRUCTURE
- FG-005a owns the minimal asynchronous adapter, schema, connection/worker lifecycle, transaction/retry law, and export/import.
- FG-005b owns reference equivalence, concurrency-envelope, cancellation, crash/reopen, checkpoint, and real-process evidence.

EPIC ACCEPTANCE
- passes the unchanged FG-004 AuthorityStore contract and history checker;
- uses the one FG-011 Asupersync runtime profile and a runtime-owned &Cx throughout;
- fsqlite default features are off; only the exact native asynchronous role features are admitted, with no C API/rusqlite/native SQLite production path or concurrent stock-SQLite opens;
- raw Connection affinity and AsyncConnection worker/channel bounds are explicit; shutdown awaits close/join and never credits Drop as proof;
- every transaction explicitly awaits commit/rollback; bounded retry restarts the whole transaction only for registered transient errors, while SnapshotTooOld triggers a fresh-snapshot decision;
- exactly one CAS winner, stable non-content version tokens across restart, body-first/head-last recovery, and export/import byte equivalence;
- declared reader/writer/checkpoint support matrix matches the exact selected FrankenSQLite revision. Writer admission is capped to proven cells; no lock-free or ten-plus implicit-writer claim is inferred;
- benchmark claims name hardware/corpus/profile and compare against a plain-filesystem reference without promoting microbenchmarks to end-to-end claims.

REFERENCE
Follow docs/ASUPERSYNC_AND_FRANKENSQLITE_INTEGRATION_PROFILE.md. If the adopted sibling release or runtime convergence is not ready, this epic remains blocked pending the owned upstream update; no substitute database/path dependency is allowed.

SCOPE
Build the final embedded AuthorityStore adapter against the upstream-converged, registry-resolvable FrankenSQLite release and FG-011 runtime profile.

DELIVERABLES
- minimal fsqlite dependency (`default-features = false`; exact native + asynchronous features only), constellation/dependency evidence, and explicit exclusion of C API, rusqlite/native SQLite, unrelated extensions, and unpublished paths;
- schema for immutable bodies/seals and repository head containing canonical bytes, exact predecessor token, monotone generation, and unique per-write ABA-safe token that is never a content hash;
- Asupersync-aware AsyncConnection ownership: Runtime-created &Cx for open/operations/close, bounded dedicated workers and command queues per declared lane/service, no per-request unbounded connection creation, explicit shutdown close/join;
- awaited begin/commit/rollback protocol and whole-transaction retry helper limited to Busy, BusyRecovery, BusySnapshot, DatabaseLocked, WriteConflict, SerializationFailure, and PageBufferCapacityExhausted when idempotent and budget remains; SnapshotTooOld requires a fresh transaction/snapshot;
- exact put-if-absent/read/exact-version-CAS/receipt operations plus canonical export/import.

ACCEPTANCE
- unchanged FG-004 contract suite passes;
- two and N admitted contenders produce exactly one CAS winner under the history checker; unsupported concurrency counts are admission-refused, not silently extrapolated;
- cancellation before dispatch, queued, executing, commit-ambiguous, reply, and close preserves the correct typed outcome and performs lookup/reconciliation where required;
- version tokens remain unique across kill/reopen and byte-identical writes;
- explicit close proves no live DB worker/thread/descriptor or unfinalized transaction; Drop-only cleanup fixture does not count as success;
- no statement-only retry, infinite retry, error-class widening, or accidental default feature.

UNIT TESTS
Schema/canonical bytes; token monotonicity/ABA; transient classification; retry budget/backoff; fresh-snapshot transition; connection affinity/pool bounds; explicit commit/rollback; cancellation phases; close/join; forbidden feature/source graph; export/import.

CONSTITUTIONAL CONSTRAINTS
One authority, one runtime, safe first-party Rust, no FFI/local path/alternate database. Current upstream mismatches block integration until the owner updates siblings; they do not authorize substitutes.

---
## PLAN-SPACE REVIEW REVISIONS (added during the pre-implementation polish pass)

### BINDING INTEGRATION PROFILE (§3 FrankenSQLite caller profile) — acceptance obligations

Per docs/ASUPERSYNC_AND_FRANKENSQLITE_INTEGRATION_PROFILE.md §3:
- Authority boundary: fsqlite has exactly two roles — (1) implement the embedded AuthorityStore over the same immutable bodies + exact predecessor-token head CAS as every backend; (2) store DISPOSABLE local projections that name their head/RCR/generation. A SQL commit does NOT publish repository state unless it IS the embedded authority operation. Projection tables/queues/caches/indexes cannot authorize, infer commit, extend retention, or decide deletion.
- Minimal surface: `fsqlite` with default-features = false and the smallest native async feature set the admission gate proves; JSON/FTS/RTree/ICU/session/RaptorQ/C-API/WASM are OFF unless a named consumer proves need. io_uring is a target profile, not a semantic dependency (portable fallback runs the same suite). The C API and concurrent stock-SQLite access are excluded from production; upstream SQLite/rusqlite only in pinned non-production differential lanes.
- Ownership: async API with a runtime-owned &Cx (no sync constructors / ad-hoc runtimes on the request path). A raw Connection is !Send+!Sync and stays on one owning worker/local lane; AsyncConnection owns a dedicated worker + bounded command channel, pooled per lane, never unbounded-per-request. Every connection/worker has owner/capacity/shutdown-budget/explicit close(&Cx)+join; drop cleanup is only a backstop. A transaction finalizes by awaited commit/rollback (drop-rollback is not abort evidence). Cancellation mid-command/commit returns typed ambiguity + does the state/outcome lookup.
- Retry law (§3.4): retry wraps the WHOLE logical transaction from a fresh snapshot; same-attempt bounded retry only for the reviewed transient family {Busy, BusyRecovery, BusySnapshot, DatabaseLocked, WriteConflict, SerializationFailure, PageBufferCapacityExhausted} subject to idempotency + budget. SnapshotTooOld needs a fresh snapshot decision (not blind in-place retry). Corruption/schema/constraint/invariant/cancellation/panic/resource-ceiling/permanent-IO are NEVER converted to "busy". Backoff is bounded, cancellation-aware, seeded/receipted, stops before the parent deadline; exhaustion returns a stable refusal with attempts/elapsed/last-error-class/remediation. The engine serializes part of commit through a commit guard — do NOT claim lock-free/unconstrained multiwriter commit.
- Concurrency envelope (§3.5): publish an explicit support matrix (1 conn/1 writer; multi-conn readers + bounded writers; same-process CAS contenders; projection-rebuild + live rw; checkpoint-under-load; crash/reopen/recovery). Do NOT claim >=10 concurrent implicit-autocommit writers until the upstream four-scenario gate proves it; cap/admission-control the writer topology to the proven envelope.

SCOPE
Prove the embedded FrankenSQLite AuthorityStore against the pure reference backend, its exact declared concurrency envelope, cancellation semantics, and real crash/reopen behavior.

MATRIX
- kill/restart before body write, after body write, after sync, before/after SQL commit/CAS, before/after acknowledgement, during checkpoint, during retry/backoff, during explicit connection close, and during process shutdown;
- one writer; readers plus bounded writers; N AuthorityStore CAS contenders; projection-style read/rebuild interference; checkpoint under load; every claimed target filesystem/profile;
- cancellation before dispatch, queued, executing, commit-ambiguous, reply-lost, retry sleep, rollback, close, and shutdown;
- transient-family and SnapshotTooOld planted errors; resource/mailbox/connection admission exhaustion;
- identical scripted histories against FG-004 reference and FrankenSQLite adapter.

ACCEPTANCE
- old-complete or new-complete at every crash point, never mixed; highest acknowledged unresolved state fails closed;
- exact one-winner histories and byte-identical outcomes/receipts versus the reference profile;
- retry replays the whole transaction only, respects remaining Cx budget, and emits stable attempt/error/remediation evidence on exhaustion;
- reopen uses known authenticated keys, never listing; no concurrent stock-SQLite open;
- explicit close/join leaves zero DB workers, threads, descriptors, transactions, reservations, or ambiguous effects;
- the report publishes the support matrix. Any unproved ten-plus implicit-writer or multi-process/checkpoint cell is unsupported/non-pass and is admission-capped in production;
- a planted statement-only retry, dropped transaction, worker leak, second-winner bug, default-feature expansion, and unsupported-writer claim are detected.

TEST ASSETS
Unit/property/history tests plus scripts/e2e/sqlite_authority_crash.sh and scripts/e2e/sqlite_authority_concurrency.sh, registered in the exact suite manifest. Real OS kill/restart evidence is required; Lab failpoints may supplement but not replace it.

E2E LOGGING
Scripts use set -euo pipefail and scripts/e2e/lib.sh. Every step emits NDJSON to stderr and an artifact with source/toolchain/constellation/fsqlite/runtime/profile identity, database/file-system parameters, connection/writer counts, seed/schedule/crash point, command, exit, duration, expected/actual head/outcome, worker/fd inventory, and artifact digests. Failures preserve database files, process logs, last state inventory, and one replay command; final records give exact pass/fail/unsupported totals.

CONSTRAINTS
No production C SQLite/rusqlite, alternate runtime, local path, first-party unsafe, broad retry, silent cleanup, second authority, or concurrency overclaim.

SCOPE
Implement the smallest real fgit-runtime vertical slice over the adopted, upstream-converged Asupersync 0.4.x constellation.

DELIVERABLES
- node AppSpec definition with deterministic compile/start order, explicit root budget/profile, typed AppHandle stop/join, and service dependency graph;
- production Cx factory using Runtime/RuntimeHandle request_cx_with_budget/try_request_cx_with_budget; capability-set narrowing at ingress and subsystem boundaries;
- standard finite request/service budgets, child meet rules, stable exhaustion/refusal vocabulary, and evidence-safe profile fingerprints;
- Outcome-preserving service adapter that does not collapse cancellation or panic/containment into ordinary errors;
- documented ownership chooser and one real demonstration service using Scope, bounded JoinSet, and actor/GenServer only where their ownership shapes apply;
- obligation policy and dependency-ordered shutdown: stop admission, request cancellation, drain, finalize/transfer obligations, explicitly close database workers, flush evidence, join root.

ACCEPTANCE
- no test-only/detached Cx constructor occurs in a production target;
- planted capability-widening and child-budget-widening attempts fail;
- no request/parser/transfer/database/background controller inherits an accidental infinite budget;
- no detached task retains publication, object, network, database, secret, runner, or billing capability;
- verification/release profile uses fail-fast obligation leak handling; any Recover profile requires durable leak evidence, health degradation, bounded cleanup, and escalation; Silent/Log-only are rejected;
- profile identity includes exact Asupersync source/version/features, worker/scheduler/queue/blocking/leak policy, target, and budget defaults;
- first real demo protocol runs under production and Lab profiles with the same typed outcomes.

UNIT TESTS
Context provenance; capability masks; nested budget meet; deadline/poll/cost exhaustion; Outcome mapping; AppSpec invalid DAG/start-stop order; bounded mailbox/JoinSet admission; reserve/commit/abort/ack; cancellation before/during/after externally observed effects; shutdown order and explicit close.

CONSTRAINTS
No compatibility wrapper that hides Asupersync semantics, alternate runtime, first-party unsafe, infinite request default, detached spawn, or unproved tree-wide restart claim. Upstream version mismatch keeps this bead blocked; it does not authorize another framework/runtime.

SCOPE
Prove the FG-011 production runtime profile under deterministic schedules and native execution. This is a distinct evidence bead so the runtime epic cannot close on implementation/demo code alone.

DETERMINISTIC CAMPAIGN
- cancel before start and at every declared await/yield across request, fan-out, actor call, reserve/commit/abort/ack, and shutdown;
- fixed worker/scheduler/budget/RNG profiles; trace identity, schedule coverage, minimized crashpack, and replay command;
- capability-widening, budget-widening, infinite-request, detached-child, mailbox/JoinSet overflow, late spawn, lost reply, and obligation-leak planted negatives;
- same demo protocol under Lab and production executors with identical typed success/error/cancelled/panicked outcomes.

NATIVE CAMPAIGN
- parked workers and wakeups; real file/socket I/O; blocking-pool task and join; signal-driven node stop; child process/task reaping; database-worker close ordering; panic containment;
- repeated start/stop and cancellation storms with bounded time/memory and zero orphan tasks, threads, descriptors, children, credentials, reservations, or publication capability;
- fail-fast verification leak policy and a separately configured Recover-with-durable-record/escalation profile; Silent and log-only are planted failures.

ACCEPTANCE
- scripts/e2e/runtime_profile_lifecycle.sh and scripts/e2e/runtime_native_shutdown.sh are registered in the exact suite manifest;
- every matrix row has pass/fail/unsupported (unsupported is non-pass), exact runtime/profile/source/toolchain/target identity, seed/schedule/fault point, resource deltas, and artifact digests;
- an injected detached authority-bearing child, planted dropped obligation, and stuck database worker are detected and prevent quiescence;
- deterministic evidence is not credited as native teardown evidence or vice versa;
- failure output contains expected/actual state, owner tree, outstanding obligations, task/thread/fd/process inventory, last logs, and minimal replay command.

E2E LOGGING
Both scripts use set -euo pipefail and scripts/e2e/lib.sh. Every step writes NDJSON to stderr and an artifact file with timestamps, command, exit, duration, identities, seed/schedule, expected/actual, and artifact digests; final records report exact rows run/passed/failed/unsupported and wall time.

GOAL
Every effect that acquires responsibility — object staging, head publication, outbox delivery, package/release upload, secret leases, workspace outputs, repair writes, agent effects — becomes a typed obligation with the normative lifecycle: Reserved to Committed to Acknowledged, or Reserved to Aborted. Fire-and-forget is not a state.

WHY / BACKGROUND
Cancellation correctness is impossible when effects are untracked: a dropped future holding a half-sent webhook or an un-reaped runner is silent corruption of the outside world. The CALM/obligation doctrine (docs/CALM_AND_OBLIGATIONS.md) makes ownership structural: must_use obligations, region close requiring settle-or-explicit-transfer, and — for externally observed effects — a distinct Acknowledged stage: commit makes the effect canonically owned; acknowledgement separately records that the recipient observed it; post-commit retry is idempotent; region close either records acknowledgement or leaves an explicit unacknowledged-effect record, never silence. The CALM registry (registries/calm_operations.tsv, 7-class closed vocabulary) determines WHERE coordination is required; obligations determine WHO owns unfinished work.

STRUCTURE: subtasks = (a) obligation core + concrete obligation types, (b) quiescence oracle + lab evidence.

ACCEPTANCE (epic)
- core obligation types from CALM section 7 exist with the trait shape from CALM section 6 (Obligation::commit yields CommittedObligation; abort; Acknowledge trait for the ack stage): ObjectAdmissionPermit, PreparedTxnSlot, HeadCasAttempt, OutboxEffectPermit, SecretLease, WorkspaceLease, RunnerSlot, RetentionPin, RepairPermit, ContextBudgetPermit, BillingReservation;
- every reserved effect reaches committed/aborted/terminally-quarantined before region close; dropping without transfer/commit/abort is a lab correctness failure and a typed production containment event;
- external APIs with weak idempotency get an explicit reconciliation state machine;
- obligation ledger replayable and linked to TxId/IntentRun;
- CALM registry class consulted for coordination decisions (a monotone op never takes the head CAS path; a head_cas_required op cannot bypass it — both directions fixture-tested, proving registry rows are load-bearing).

CONSTITUTIONAL CONSTRAINTS (AGENTS.md; non-negotiable)
- Pure Rust, edition 2024, dated-nightly pin from rust-toolchain.toml; every first-party crate carries #![forbid(unsafe_code)]; no C/C++ FFI, no C Git/libgit2/JGit/Dulwich/gix, no hidden subprocess fallback. Upstream Git binaries are pinned, sandboxed differential ORACLES only (never production).
- Asupersync is the sole async runtime (no Tokio/async-std/smol). Long-lived work owns children via regions; cancellation is request -> drain -> finalize; effects use typed obligations (Reserved -> Committed -> Acknowledged, or Reserved -> Aborted).
- Closed dependency universe: every crate (incl. transitive, enforced via Cargo.lock scan) must match an active allow row in registries/dependency_policy.tsv. No build scripts/proc macros without a constitutional exception. No network during builds.
- Final-abstraction slices only: no empty crates, no HashMap-pretending-to-be-storage, no fixture-only parser wired as production API. A subset is fine when its unsupported surface is a typed refusal.
- Claim lattice (invariant > proof > bounded model > statistical > SLO > benchmark): never describe this work as stronger than its evidence. Record disproven hypotheses in docs/NEGATIVE_EVIDENCE_LEDGER.md + registries/negative_evidence.tsv.
